    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0094" n="84" xml:id="pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.92/259: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-02-21T20:00:00-05:00">February 21,
                            1941—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. According to a telegram of February 15 from Vichy,<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d87-f1"/> based upon information supplied by the French Government,
                    the French Ambassador at Tokyo recently refused to continue the negotiations for
                    a Thai-Indochinese settlement unless the Thai attitude be moderated; a notable
                    improvement in the Japanese attitude resulted; the Japanese Chargé d’Affaires at
                    Vichy has informed the French Government that the Japanese Minister at Bangkok
                    has been instructed to insist on moderation of the Thai attitude and on
                    withdrawal of Thai troops who recently crossed the Mekong in Luang Prabang.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
